Changelog
---------

7.0.0
~~~~~

2026-10-31 • [full history]

**Breaking Changes**

- Drop support for Python 3.9 and 3.10.
- [core] Changed pattern matching mechanism from using ``path.match() to
path.full_match()``. Users must update patterns to glob-like syntax: e.g.,
`*.py` to `**/*.py`. (`#1101
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1101>`__)
- [core] Added FileAttribEvent and DirAttribEvent for file and directory
metadata modifications (such as permissions or timestamps), separate from
content modifications. These events no longer trigger ``on_modified()``;
implement ``on_attrib()`` to handle them. On Windows 10 (1709+) and Windows
Server 2016+, ReadDirectoryChangesExW is used to differentiate attribute
modifications, with fallback to ReadDirectoryChangesW on older versions or
unsupported file shares. (`#260
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/260>`__)
- [watchmedo] Changed the default ``--patterns value from "*" to "**"``, so
the default matches absolute paths at any depth under the ``full_match()``
semantics introduced by #1101, and updated the CLI help text and docs to
the ``**/`` glob syntax. (`#1212
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/1212>`__)

**Other Changes**

- Add support for Python 3.15 (`#1226
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/1226>`__)
- [core] Add context manager support to Observer class. The observer can
now be used with a with statement for automatic start/stop management.
(`#1090 <https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1149>`__)
- [core] Add support for the follow_symlink keyword argument to
ObservedWatch. (`#1086
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1086>`__)
- [core] Added the ignore_policy argument to PatternMatchingEventHandler
and RegexMatchingEventHandler to configure multi-path event filtering
(moves/renames). PatternMatchingEventHandler is now strict by default,
aligning with RegexMatchingEventHandler. (`#412
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/412>`__, `#423
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/423>`__)
- [core] Added the ``watchdog.utils.Seconds`` type alias and used it for
the time-duration parameters (timeout, polling_interval, kill_after, ...)
instead of documenting the unit in each docstring. Duration parameters
previously hinted as int now accept float.
- [core] Adjust ``Observer.schedule() path type annotation to reflect the
pathlib.Path`` support. (`#1096
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1096>`__)
- [core] Allow scheduling watches on individual files in
``Observer.schedule()``. (`#1034
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/issues/1034>`__)
- [core] Call ``task_done() for the stop sentinel in dispatch_events() to
prevent join()`` from hanging. (`#1159
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1159>`__)
- [core] ``case_sensitive=False matching now really ignores case on Python
<`` 3.13. The ``PurePath.full_match() fallback compiled its regex without
re.IGNORECASE``, so only the patterns were lower-cased and a path such as
``FOO.PY never matched **/*.py``. (`#1263
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1263>`__)
- [core] ``dispatch_events()`` no longer re-adds a watch that
``unschedule()`` removed, which leaked one _handlers entry per watch that
had an event in flight. (`#1261
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1261>`__)
- [core] Do not retain an event handler when ``Observer.schedule()`` fails
to create or start its emitter.
- [core] EventEmitter and EventDispatcher reject a bool timeout. bool
subclasses int, so ``timeout=True was stored and treated as 1.0`` seconds.
(`#1287 <https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1287>`__)
- [core] Fixed ``generate_sub_moved_events()`` corrupting paths when the
directory name appears multiple times in the path. (`#1158
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1158>`__)
- [core] ObservedWatch equality now includes follow_symlink, so scheduling
a path a second time with a different follow_symlink value no longer
collapses onto the first watch and silently drops the request. (`#1262
<https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1262>`__)
- [core] RegexMatchingEventHandler no longer matches its regexes against an
empty destination path for events that are not moves. Since events became
dataclasses, ``hasattr(event, "dest_path")`` is always true, so a regex
matching the empty string (e.g. ``^(?!.*\.pyc$).*$``) let every event
through, and such an ignore regex dropped every event.
PatternMatchingEventHandler had the same check.
- [core] ``remove_handler_for_watch()`` no longer re-adds a watch that
``unschedule()`` removed, which leaked one empty _handlers entry per call.
(`#1285 <https://github.com/gorakhargosh/watchdog/pull/1285>`__)


